#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063969 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064193 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a1a59be3-afee-56bd-a554-037c5ad99f83" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Equations When the Variables are Separate"}] :question/id #uuid "3b855590-1e40-5dee-a518-0211c627281e" :question/math-academy-id "e-13909" :question/problem "Solve for $x$ where $2x - y = 5y - z$." :question/worked-solution "We need to isolate $x$, so we will treat the other variables $y$ and $z$ as constants. We can use the addition and multiplication principles to solve for $x$.\n\nFirst, we add $y$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 2x - y &= 5y - z \\\\[5pt] 2x - y + y &= 5y - z + y \\\\[5pt] 2x &= 6y - z \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we divide both sides by $2$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 2x &= 6y - z \\\\[5pt] \\dfrac {2x} 2 &= \\dfrac{6y - z} {2} \\\\[5pt] x &= \\dfrac{6y - z} {2} \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063970 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064194 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "202c3d83-dd90-539a-8e22-9689e936e308" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Equations When the Variables are Multiplied"}] :question/id #uuid "0fa3b7ba-5b22-5ba4-9898-0bdfee684683" :question/math-academy-id "e-13910" :question/problem "The energy $E$ of a body at rest is related to its mass $m$ by the equation $E=mC$, where $C$ is a constant. What is an expression for the mass ($m$) in terms of the energy ($E$) and the constant ($C$)?" :question/worked-solution "We need to isolate $m$, so we will treat the other variables $E$ and $C$ as constants. Since $m$ is being multiplied by $C$, we need to divide both sides of the equation by $C$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE &= mC \\\\\n\\frac{E}{C} &= \\frac{mC}{C} \\\\\n\\frac{E}{C} &= m\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus,\n\n$$\nm = \\dfrac E C\n$$\n\n**Note:** This result assumes that\n\n$$\nC\\neq 0\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186063971 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064195 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a9f58b68-b706-5e6b-b2a4-851517a1db28" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Equations Requiring Manipulation of Binomials"}] :question/id #uuid "6cf331f4-6251-53ff-889b-7762f381d087" :question/math-academy-id "e-13914" :question/problem "The total energy $E$ of a body moving with a (squared) velocity $V$ can be approximated using the equation $E = mC + \\dfrac{1}{2}mV$. Find an expression for $V$ in terms of the other quantities." :question/worked-solution "We need to isolate $V$, so we will treat the other variables $E$, $C$, and $m$ as constants. We can use the addition and multiplication principles to solve for $V$.\n\nFirst, we subtract $mC$ from both sides of the equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE &= mC + \\frac{1}{2}mV \\\\\nE - mC &= mC + \\frac{1}{2}mV - mC \\\\\nE - mC &= \\frac{1}{2}mV\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we multiply by $2$ to get rid of the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nE - mC &= \\frac{1}{2}mV \\\\\n2 \\cdot (E - mC) &= 2 \\cdot \\frac{1}{2}mV \\\\\n2(E - mC) &= mV\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide by $m$ to get $V$ alone:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2(E - mC) &= mV \\\\\n(2(E - mC))/(m) &= \\frac{mV}{m} \\\\\n(2(E - mC))/(m) &= V\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus,\n\n$$\nV = \\dfrac{2(E-mC)}{m}\n$$\n\n**Note:** This result assumes that\n\n$$\nm\\neq 0\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064782 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186064193 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a1a59be3-afee-56bd-a554-037c5ad99f83" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Equations When the Variables are Separate"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bde9818d-72ce-5f72-9760-55b8684dbcf7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "c = 9b + 6a + 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062750} {:answer/id #uuid "06fee15e-7570-542a-962c-712a4988ef6d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "c = 9b + 3a" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062751} {:answer/id #uuid "1d48f386-b718-5a37-9705-1bd64cec3ed9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "c = 9b + 6a - 2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062752} {:answer/id #uuid "3a18d6cc-753f-52ed-8d77-de41892475a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "c = \\frac{9b + 6a}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062753} {:answer/id #uuid "6c5ea4ce-83f8-5f1d-b212-8f0b8eaed3b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "c = \\frac{9b - 6a}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062754}] :answer-field/id #uuid "892f2275-2bc5-559b-b11e-c37f8b2dc7b7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186062749}] :question/id #uuid "8065c427-1ef3-5709-a373-7fc538897b32" :question/math-academy-id "q-44312" :question/problem "Make $c$ the subject of the equation $-6a = 9b - 2c$."}]}
